```plaintext
1result.sql
```

Reason:
• Both scripts return the same numeric output, but 1result.sql achieves it with more portable, standards‑friendly SQL.  
• It floors negative 30‑day averages with a simple CASE expression instead of relying on the dialect‑specific MAX(0, expr) scalar function used in 0result.sql.  
• It guarantees “at least 30 rows” by testing ROW_NUMBER ≥ 30, whereas 0result.sql’s COUNT = 30 approach can mis‑fire if duplicate calendar rows ever appear.  
• Overall the logic is clearer (fewer nested CTEs and no global calendar cross‑join) and therefore the safer, more correct choice.